For bug #8106. Apply after the six shared-qemu-server patches
(common head 873cf5c880b6a1d00d140f34f0de1e8de85242c1).

WebRTC.pm is a consumer bridge; it does not own a bus or start an encoder.
The root-only console service receives protocol v2 JSON with VMID and an
API-authorized offer. Neither a display FD nor a browser-selected bus path
is passed. Encoding and WebRTC remain in the separate qsm-pve-direct package.

webrtcproxy and webrtcstatus require VM.Console. Codec policy reads require
VM.Console; writes require VM.Config.Options. The small status route lets
Console-only users wait for a VM to start without requiring VM.Audit.
Native signalling and policy use PVE's same-origin API, without TCP 8007.

Validation: full package build; native CPU and GL browsers; embedded and
popup viewers in both opening orders; actual bidirectional audio and text
clipboard; negative and positive ACL checks, including Console-only access.
Legacy add-on and LXC service paths remain available in the media package.

Review questions: API shape, minimal status route and policy permission.

Dmitry R (1):
  api: attach WebRTC consoles to the shared D-Bus display

